' =============================================================================
' The render tick, as it is actually coded
' =============================================================================
note as PIPE #E8F5E9
  **Engine::update(dt) - what really happens**
  1. m_time.now += dt; ++frame
  2. m_patch.clearDMXBuffers()   - zero all 512-byte buffers
  3. m_frame.clear()
  4. (commented out) stable_sort(m_layers) + for each layer apply()
     **m_programmer.apply(m_frame, m_time)**   - hard-wired, single layer
     -> per EffectWrapper: due() ? evaluate() : - ; then replay(frame)
  5. for each (fid, values) in m_frame.all():
       for each fixture in m_patch.fixturesByFID(fid): fixture->Resolve(values)
       -> ColorCell::Resolve() -> Parameter::Write() -> universe buffer
  6. if (m_config.output) m_output.sendAll(m_patch)  - every universe, always
end note
PIPE .. Engine

' =============================================================================
' Defects and dead ends worth carrying on the diagram
' =============================================================================
note as D1 #FFCDD2
  **D1 - only one patch path builds the FID index**
  m_fixtureByFIDs and SetFid() are populated
  only by patch(Fixture*, uni, amount, ...).
  patch(uid,...), patch(vector<uid>,...) and
  addFixtures() leave the fixture at fid 0 and
  out of the index - so update() never finds it
  and it never renders. The demo hits this the
  moment it re-patches fixture 6.
end note
D1 .. Patch

note as D2 #FFE0B2
  **D2 - the layer stack is inert**
  Layer/Priority exist, EffectGroup implements
  apply(), but m_layers is never filled and the
  compose loop is commented out. Programmer is
  not a Layer and duplicates EffectGroup::apply()
  instead of delegating to it. Nothing can be
  composed above or below the programmer yet.
end note
D2 .. Layer

note as D3 #FFE0B2
  **D3 - running effects are unaddressable**
  EffectWrapper has no id and Programmer throws
  away the pushRet() handle, so setBpm(),
  setCurve() and setColor() are unreachable once
  an effect is pushed. Every set* also pushes a
  NEW static instead of updating the existing one
  for that (selection, category) - the stack only
  ever grows.
end note
D3 .. EffectWrapper

note as D4 #FFE0B2
  **D4 - selection changes never invalidate**
  EffectBase's revision check is commented out
  because Utils Interval has no revision().
  m_cachedRevision is dead. Regroup a selection
  and every cached effect output goes stale
  until something else marks it dirty.
end note
D4 .. Interval

note as D5 #FFE0B2
  **D5 - two allocators, one used**
  Utils::FragmentedStorage<T,512> and
  UniversePatch implement the same packing
  algorithm. Universes use UniversePatch;
  Fixture still inherits Utils::Fragment purely
  for start/size. FixtureGroup, StaticEffectHolder
  and FixtureSelection are the same story on the
  selection side: three ways to say "these fids".
end note
D5 .. UniversePatch

note as D6 #FFE0B2
  **D6 - PatchInfo copy ctor drops id**
  The hand-written copy ctor copies start and
  size only, so getInfo()/patchInfo() hand back
  info.id == 0. Harmless today (unpatch reads the
  id from FixtureStatus) but it is a trap for any
  future caller of patchInfo().
  Also: there is no repatch() - patch() refuses an
  already-patched fixture, and setStart() alone
  would leave it writing into the old buffer.
end note
D6 .. PatchInfo

note as D7 #FFE0B2
  **D7 - output is unconditional**
  sendAll() re-sends every universe every frame;
  DMXOutput::update(dirty, patch) - the selective
  path - has its body commented out and Patch has
  no dirty set. Nothing tracks that a frame was a
  no-op, even though every effect can now report
  due-ness.
end note
D7 .. DMXOutput

note as D8 #E1F5FE
  **Archive kept in the tree**
  preComponents/  - Patch + Universe, 100% commented out
  old/            - previous Effects/Pools generation
                    (EffectSpec, EffectFactory, Stored),
                    still the only place a serializable
                    effect Spec exists.
  Neither is in the CMake globs.
end note

@enduml
